      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey quick question... i'm an architect and i've been staying at this new development in hudson yards lately. the smart hvac system in my unit is making this ultra low hum. i know it's technically \"sub-audible\" but i can literally feel it in my chest. it's making it impossible to focus and i feel super on edge. have you heard anything about these high-tech building systems being tuned to specific frequencies for \"occupant management\" or something? it feels way too intentional.",
